      "beta": "Success iff every head path terminates at root; on active-color revisit report the least ordered nonterminating start, including tails.",
      "cost": "Let n be token count after preflight. Both small branches use O(n^2) walk work with n<=64 and O(1) cycle-phase auxiliary storage. Large annotation calls use at most 4n walk steps then optional O(n) reversed adjacency/BFS. Large conversion calls use at most 2n head transitions and O(n) color storage, allocated on every n>64 cycle-phase entry; no reverse rows or queue. Conversion separately retains its heads Vec. Diagnostic strings add error-path allocations. Parsing, normalization and conversion edits have their own costs; no whole-module linearity claim follows.",
      "domain": "Finite validated functional head maps; successful allocation. Annotation and conversion retain different empty/self-head rules.",
      "evidence_status": "current_source_local_evidence_linked_transfer_wave25; historical_timing_not_rebound",
      "id": "bfs-conversion",
      "mechanism": "functional-graph coloring realizing root-reachability equivalence; no runtime BFS",
      "premises": [
        "Preserve original parsing, range, root-label and root-count order.",
        "Completed paths leave no active colors; each head is followed at most twice in the large branch.",
        "BFS remains a mathematical reachability reference, not a current conversion call.",
        "Original before binding is historical 34811b; wave25 comparison fd540 already contains models."
      ],
      "rejected_near_match": "First cycle member is not first failed start; an earlier tail must retain its diagnostic. Reusing a completed suffix must not report a cycle.",
